<body>

    <h1 id="main-heading">Web Technology</h1>

    <h2>Introduction to HTML</h2>

    <p id="intro" title="Introduction to HTML">
        HTML stands for
        <strong>HyperText Markup Language</strong>.
        It is a markup language used to create and structure
        web pages.
        HTML is used to create the basic structure of a web page.
        It uses tags and elements to organize the content of a
        webpage.
    </p>

    <h2>Elements of HTML</h2>

    <p>
        An HTML element generally consists of an opening tag,
        content, and a closing tag.
    </p>

    <p>
        Example:
        <b>&lt;p&gt;Welcome to HTML&lt;/p&gt;</b>
    </p>

    <h2>Basic Structure of HTML</h2>

    <p>
        A basic HTML document contains the
        <strong>&lt;html&gt;</strong>,
        <strong>&lt;head&gt;</strong> and
        <strong>&lt;body&gt;</strong> elements.
    </p>

    <h2>HTML Tags and Attributes</h2>

    <p title="HTML attribute example">
        HTML tags define the structure of webpage content.
        Attributes provide additional information about
        HTML elements.
    </p>

    <p>
        Example:
        <b>&lt;p title="Example"&gt;This is a paragraph.&lt;/p&gt;</b>
    </p>

    <p>
        In the above example, <strong>title</strong> is an attribute
        and <strong>"Example"</strong> is its value.
    </p>

    <h2>Basic HTML Tags</h2>

    <p>
        Basic HTML tags include
        <strong>&lt;html&gt;</strong>,
        <strong>&lt;head&gt;</strong>,
        <strong>&lt;title&gt;</strong>,
        <strong>&lt;body&gt;</strong> and
        <strong>&lt;p&gt;</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>HTML Headings</h2>

    <p>
        HTML provides six levels of headings from
        <strong>&lt;h1&gt;</strong> to
        <strong>&lt;h6&gt;</strong>.
    </p>

    <h3>This is an Example of H3 Heading</h3>

    <h2>HTML Paragraphs</h2>

    <p>
        The <strong>&lt;p&gt;</strong> tag is used to create
        paragraphs in an HTML document.
    </p>

    <p>
        Paragraphs are used to organize text and make webpage
        content easier to read.
    </p>

    <h2>Text Formatting Tags</h2>

    <p>
        <b>This is bold text using the &lt;b&gt; tag.</b>
    </p>

    <p>
        <i>This is italic text using the &lt;i&gt; tag.</i>
    </p>

    <p>
        <u>This is underlined text using the &lt;u&gt; tag.</u>
    </p>

    <p>
        <strong>This is important text using the &lt;strong&gt; tag.</strong>
    </p>

    <p>
        <em>This is emphasized text using the &lt;em&gt; tag.</em>
    </p>

    <p>
        <small>This is small text using the &lt;small&gt; tag.</small>
    </p>

    <p>
        <ins>This is inserted text using the &lt;ins&gt; tag.</ins>
    </p>

    <p>
        <del>This is deleted text using the &lt;del&gt; tag.</del>
    </p>

    <p>
        Chemical Formula:
        H<sub>2</sub>O
    </p>

    <p>
        Mathematical Expression:
        X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup>
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li><b>Advantages of HTML:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Easy to learn and use</li>
                <li>Supported by all browsers</li>
                <li>Lightweight</li>
                <li>Integrates well with other languages</li>
            </ul>
        </li>

        <li><b>Disadvantages of HTML:</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Limited security features</li>
                <li>Not suitable for dynamic content on its own</li>
                <li>Requires CSS/JavaScript for complex styling and functionality</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Conclusion</h2>

    <p id="conclusion" title="HTML Unit I Conclusion">
        HTML is the foundation of web development. Understanding
        HTML tags, elements, attributes, headings, paragraphs and
        text formatting is an important first step in learning
        Web Technology.
    </p>

</body>

